{"reference":"Psalms 128","book":"Psalms","chapter":128,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Surrounding Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The larger collection around this psalm includes communal memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile, alongside thanksgiving for return, festival praise, Torah meditation, and Songs of Ascents oriented toward worship. This broader setting is debated, but it places Psalm 128 within a sequence concerned with communal worship as well as individual blessing.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 133:1-3","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_128_1d331a8ddef63996d71dad8d"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}